# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; .env.example is not.
#
# No spaces around "=" — a leading space becomes part of the value in most
# dotenv parsers and surfaces later as a confusing authentication failure.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe — TEST MODE. Everything in M1–M3 uses these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxx
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe — LIVE MODE. Leave unset until the M5 real-card decline demo.
#
# Run pnpm --filter @pay-agent/store live-decline-check <pm_id> <balance> <amount> once this
# is set (see the script's header for the enrollment step that comes before it).
#
# This is a deliberately separate variable, never a swapped value of the test
# key, so live mode cannot be entered by accident. Two guards depend on it:
#
#   1. The live path refuses to run unless the intended charge EXCEEDS the
#      enrolled balance — so the only live outcome is a decline, and no money
#      moves.
#   2. The deployed build FAILS AT STARTUP if this is present. The hosted demo
#      is test-mode only; a public URL and live card rails must never meet.
#
# Only ever set this on the local laptop, never in a deployment environment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRIPE_LIVE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gift-card code pepper.
#
# A pepper is not stored beside the data, so a database leak alone does not
# permit offline enumeration of card codes. Required in production; a clearly
# labelled development fallback is used when unset outside production.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GIFT_CARD_CODE_PEPPER=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram approval bot (optional). Chat-based Approve/Deny instead of the web
# inbox at /activity. Create a bot with @BotFather to get the token; message
# your bot once, then GET https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/getUpdates to
# read your chat id.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slack approval bot (optional). Same idea, in a Slack channel via Socket Mode
# (no public URL needed). Create a Slack app at https://api.slack.com/apps
# with Socket Mode + the chat:write bot scope.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=
# SLACK_CHANNEL_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp approval bot (optional, pay-agent Cloud pro-plan only — see
# apps/agent/scripts/whatsapp-bot.ts). Needs a Meta Cloud API app and a
# pay-agent Cloud tenant API key upgraded to the "pro" plan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PAY_AGENT_CLOUD_URL=
# PAY_AGENT_CLOUD_API_KEY=
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_TO=
# WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
